    '{"\$schema":"https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema","\$id":"https://trusttasks.org/spec/hcp/delegations/list/0.1","title":"HCP — List Delegations — payload","description":"The request payload of the HCP 2.0-draft-3 List delegations operation (Delegated Authorization Profile, HCP 17.2; `GET /v2/delegations` in HCP 9.2, 9.4.13): a Management Client, acting for the Context Subject or a delegate, lists the delegations it may see. HCP defines no request schema for this operation; the `status` parameter comes from HCP 9.4.13, and the result follows the delegations-result shape HCP publishes for the same draft. The outer document members (id, type, issuer, recipient, issuedAt, expiresAt, proof) are owned by the framework — SPEC §6.3. Every maxLength, maxItems and maxProperties in this schema is a Trust Tasks framework bound (SPEC §7.3 item 19), not an HCP requirement; so is every minLength or minItems of 1 on a member HCP\'s own schema allows to be empty.","type":"object","additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"accessToken":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":8192,"description":"The Management Client\'s HCP access token (HCP 9.3), carried unchanged. HCP\'s HTTP Binding sends it as a Bearer token; this member carries it in the document. The provider validates it exactly as over HTTP and treats it as opaque. The maxLength is a framework bound, not an HCP requirement. OPTIONAL: where it is absent, the provider authenticates the request\'s `issuer` VID, by the REQUIRED request proof, as a Management Client the Authorizing Principal enrolled (HCP 3.2.3), and refuses any other issuer with permissionDenied; where it is present, the token rules apply unchanged. Pending HCP confirmation (question 56)."},"status":{"type":"string","enum":["ended"],"description":"HCP query parameter `status` (HCP 9.4.13), whose one defined value is `ended`. Absent returns only the delegations that hold; `ended` returns the delegations that have ended as well as those that hold (\\"with ended ones where `status=ended` is asked\\", HCP 9.4.13), pending HCP confirmation (question 31)."}}}';

/// As [payloadSchemaJson], for the success-response variant.
const String responsePayloadSchemaJson =
    '{"\$schema":"https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema","\$ref":"#/\$defs/Response","\$defs":{"Response":{"\$anchor":"response","title":"HCP — List Delegations — response payload","type":"object","additionalProperties":false,"required":["delegations"],"description":"The delegations the caller may see (HCP 9.4.13, 17.2). Not paginated (HCP 9.4.13). Failures use trust-task-error, not this shape.","properties":{"delegations":{"type":"array","items":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/Delegation"},"description":"HCP `delegations` (HCP 9.4.13): every delegation for the Context Subject, for a Management Client acting for them; the delegations naming the delegate, and the sub-delegations that delegate appointed (pending HCP confirmation, question 32), for one acting for a delegate. An ended delegation carries `ended` (HCP 17.2, 17.6). Empty when there are none."}}},"Delegation":{"type":"object","additionalProperties":true,"required":["delegationId","subject","delegate","relationship","basis","scope","term"],"description":"One natural person\'s authority to act as Authorizing Principal for the Context Subject (HCP 17.2). The Authorization Service establishes it and the provider holds its record; neither the Context Subject nor the delegate may change it, and a change is a new delegation (HCP 17.2).","properties":{"delegationId":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/Urn","description":"Stable for the life of the delegation; named by every grant issued under it and by audit events (HCP 17.2)."},"subject":{"type":"object","additionalProperties":true,"required":["id"],"description":"The Context Subject (HCP 17.2).","properties":{"id":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":2048,"description":"The Context Subject\'s identifier."}}},"delegate":{"type":"object","additionalProperties":true,"required":["id","name"],"description":"The delegate: a natural person, with a name the Context Subject can recognize (HCP 17.1, 17.2).","properties":{"id":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":2048,"description":"The delegate\'s identifier."},"name":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":1024,"description":"A name the Context Subject can recognize."}}},"relationship":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":2048,"pattern":"^(parent-or-guardian|legal-guardian|attorney-in-fact|caregiver|[a-zA-Z][a-zA-Z0-9+.-]*:\\\\S+)\$","description":"The delegate\'s relationship to the Context Subject: a value registered in HCP A.1 (`parent-or-guardian`, `legal-guardian`, `attorney-in-fact`, `caregiver`) or an absolute URI. It confers nothing by itself; `scope` sets what the delegate may do (HCP 17.2). Distinct from an entry\'s reserved `subject.relationship` (HCP 11.3). The pattern admits the slug or an absolute URI\'s outline only: it carries no `format: uri`, which would refuse every slug, so checking that a custom value is a well-formed absolute URI, as HCP\'s prose requires (HCP A.3), is the consumer\'s check."},"basis":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/DelegationBasis","description":"What the authority rests on, and how the Authorization Service established it (HCP 17.3)."},"scope":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/DelegationScope","description":"The categories and actions the delegate may authorize (HCP 17.4)."},"term":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/DelegationTerm","description":"When the delegation ends (HCP 17.2)."},"mayDelegate":{"type":"boolean","description":"True where the delegate may appoint a sub-delegate (HCP 17.10). Absent means false. Recorded by the Authorization Service (HCP 17.2)."},"ended":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/DelegationEnded","description":"Absent while the delegation holds; set when it ends, with the reason (HCP 17.6)."}}},"DelegationEnded":{"type":"object","additionalProperties":true,"required":["at","reason"],"description":"How and when a delegation ended (HCP 17.6). The member name `at` is HCP\'s own, carried verbatim.","properties":{"at":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/Instant","description":"When the delegation ended (HCP 17.2, 17.6)."},"reason":{"type":"string","enum":["majority","expiry","basis-ended","relinquished","ended-by-subject","parent-ended","ended-by-delegate"],"description":"Why it ended (HCP 17.6). HCP\'s own values, carried verbatim."}}},"Instant":{"type":"string","format":"date-time","description":"An RFC 3339 instant."},"DelegationTerm":{"type":"object","additionalProperties":true,"required":["endsAt","atMajority"],"description":"When a delegation ends: at `endsAt`, and at the Context Subject\'s age of majority where `atMajority` is true (HCP 17.2).","properties":{"endsAt":{"type":["string","null"],"format":"date-time","description":"When the delegation ends; null where no end is known (HCP 17.2)."},"atMajority":{"type":"boolean","description":"True where the delegation ends at the Context Subject\'s age of majority, which the Authorization Service determines under the law that applies (HCP 17.2)."}}},"DelegationScope":{"type":"object","additionalProperties":true,"required":["categories","actions"],"description":"The categories and actions a delegate may authorize; every category is named, with no wildcard (HCP 17.4).","properties":{"categories":{"type":"array","minItems":1,"maxItems":256,"items":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/Category"},"description":"The categories in scope (HCP 17.4). The maxItems is a framework bound, not an HCP requirement."},"actions":{"type":"array","minItems":1,"maxItems":2,"uniqueItems":true,"items":{"type":"string","enum":["read","write"]},"description":"The actions in scope (HCP 17.2, 6.1.5)."}}},"Category":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":2048,"pattern":"^([a-z][a-z0-9_]*|[a-zA-Z][a-zA-Z0-9+.-]*:\\\\S+)\$","description":"An HCP context category (HCP 4.5), the primary unit of access control: either a slug from HCP\'s category registry, such as `general_preferences` or `health_context`, or a custom category written as an absolute URI under a domain its definer controls. A custom category is not portable between providers without bilateral agreement (HCP 4.5). The pattern admits the slug or an absolute URI\'s outline only: it carries no `format: uri`, which would refuse every slug, so checking that a custom value is a well-formed absolute URI, as HCP\'s prose requires (HCP A.3), is the consumer\'s check."},"DelegationBasis":{"type":"object","additionalProperties":true,"required":["method","description","establishedBy","establishedAt"],"description":"What a delegation\'s authority rests on (HCP 17.3). Where `method` is `evidence`, `evidence` is present with at least one item; `parent` is present exactly where `method` is `delegated` (HCP 17.3, 17.10). Those rules are not checked by the schema: the registry\'s Rust generator does not support `if`/`then`/`else`, so a validator does not check them.","properties":{"method":{"type":"string","enum":["appointed","attested","evidence","delegated","unspecified"],"description":"How the authority was established (HCP 17.3). `unspecified` is used only for a delegation converted from HCP v1 and MUST NOT be presented to anyone as `attested` (HCP 17.3, 17.8)."},"description":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":4096,"description":"What the authority rests on, shown to the Context Subject and the delegate (HCP 17.3). The maxLength is a framework bound, not an HCP requirement."},"parent":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/Urn","description":"For a sub-delegation (`method` `delegated`), the delegation it came from (HCP 17.10)."},"evidence":{"type":"array","maxItems":16,"items":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/EvidenceItem"},"description":"The evidence presented, for `method` `evidence`: a credential of guardianship, a court order, a power of attorney. A Verifiable Credential is held whole, as an entry\'s evidence item is (HCP 17.3, 4.2.2). The maxItems is a framework bound, not an HCP requirement."},"covers":{"type":"array","maxItems":256,"items":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/Category"},"description":"The High-sensitivity and custom categories the basis extends to; only these may be in `scope` (HCP 17.4). The maxItems is a framework bound, not an HCP requirement."},"establishedBy":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":2048,"description":"The Authorization Service that established the delegation (HCP 17.2)."},"establishedAt":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/Instant","description":"When the delegation was established (HCP 17.2)."}}},"EvidenceItem":{"type":"object","additionalProperties":true,"required":["role","type"],"description":"One evidence item (HCP 4.2.2). An item of a type the provider does not recognize is preserved and never raises assurance (HCP A.3). An item whose type is `verifiable-credential` MUST carry `credential`, an object with `@context`, `type`, `issuer` and `credentialSubject`, held whole as its issuer secured it (HCP 4.2.2). This rule is stated here and not as a schema conditional: the registry\'s Rust generator does not support `if`/`then`/`else`, so a validator does not check it.","properties":{"role":{"type":"string","enum":["content","supports"],"description":"`content`: the item\'s credential is the entry\'s content (VC Evidence Profile). `supports`: the item backs content stated elsewhere in the entry (HCP 4.2.2)."},"type":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":2048,"description":"The evidence type: `verifiable-credential`, or a URI (HCP 4.2.2, A.3)."},"credential":{"description":"The credential: for `verifiable-credential`, a W3C Verifiable Credential with `@context`, `type`, `issuer` and `credentialSubject`, whose own data model governs its contents (HCP 4.2.2, 14.2)."},"verification":{"type":"object","additionalProperties":true,"required":["result","at"],"description":"The provider\'s record of its most recent verification of the credential (HCP 4.2.2). Set only by the provider.","properties":{"result":{"type":"string","enum":["verified","failed"],"description":"The outcome."},"at":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/Instant","description":"When the provider verified."},"by":{"type":"string","enum":["provider","trust-domain"],"description":"Who verified: the provider, or the Context Subject\'s trust domain under end-to-end encrypted storage (HCP 4.8). HCP\'s own values, carried verbatim."}}}}},"Urn":{"type":"string","pattern":"^urn:uuid:[0-9a-fA-F]{8}-[0-9a-fA-F]{4}-[0-9a-fA-F]{4}-[0-9a-fA-F]{4}-[0-9a-fA-F]{12}\$","description":"An HCP identifier: a UUID in `urn:uuid:` form, of any UUID version (HCP 4.2), as HCP uses for entry, grant, directive and retrieval identifiers."}}}';

/// The SPEC §7.2 policy for the request variant, taken from this
/// specification's front matter.
///
/// Pass it to [consumeInbound] — items 5b, 7 and 8 are per-specification and
/// cannot be derived from the document alone, and item 2 needs the schema it
/// carries.
const SpecPolicy spec = SpecPolicy(
  typeUri: typeUri,
  isBearer: false,
  isProofRequired: true,
  isRecipientRequired: true,
  isIssuedAtRequired: true,
  payloadSchema: payloadSchemaJson,
);

/// The SPEC §7.2 policy for the success-response variant.
///
/// `isRecipientRequired` tracks the *issuer* party's requirement, because a
/// response swaps the parties (§7.3 item 5).
const SpecPolicy responseSpec = SpecPolicy(
  typeUri: responseTypeUri,
  isBearer: false,
  isProofRequired: true,
  isRecipientRequired: true,
  isIssuedAtRequired: true,
  payloadSchema: responsePayloadSchemaJson,
  maxDocumentBytes: 2097152,
);
